.TH A2WCRECALC\-DMS 1 "2026-07-06" "a2tools 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
a2wcrecalc\-dms \- \fBa2wcrecalc\fR plus \fBdocker\-mailserver\fR mapping files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B a2wcrecalc\-dms
.RB [ \-d " " \fIDMS_DIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBa2wcrecalc\-dms\fR behaves exactly like \fBa2wcrecalc\fR(1) and then
additionally generates the per\-domain mapping files used by
\fBdocker\-mailserver\fR (\fBhttps://github.com/docker\-mailserver/docker\-mailserver\fR)
to discover which virtual host each incoming connection should be
routed to.
.PP
All arguments are named flags. The \fIdocker\-mailserver\fR directory
is selected in this order: \fB\-d\fR / \fB\-\-dir\fR, then the
\fBDMS_DIR\fR environment variable, then the value of \fBDMS_DIR\fR
read from \fB/etc/a2tools/a2tools.conf\fR (or any
\fI*.conf\fR under \fB/etc/a2tools/a2tools.conf.d/\fR), then the podmgr
layout \fB/srv/podmgr/compose/dms\fR, and finally the built\-in default
\fB/opt/compose/docker\-mailserver\fR. Only directories that exist are
considered. The mapping files are written to \fIDMS_DIR\fB/config\fR, or to
\fIDMS_DIR\fB/data/config\fR when the stack uses the podmgr layout.
.PP
The certificates those files point at live under the root\-only
\fB/etc/letsencrypt\fR. When the stack belongs to a non\-root user (the
owner of \fIDMS_DIR\fB/compose.yaml\fR, i.e. root inside a rootless
container), \fBa2wcrecalc\-dms\fR grants that user read access to each
mapped certificate with \fBsetfacl\fR(1). The certbot deploy hook
re\-grants it after every renewal, because renewed private keys are
written with mode 0600.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " " \fIDMS_DIR\fR
Path to the \fBdocker\-mailserver\fR mount directory.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the embedded usage text and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DMS_DIR
Fallback path to the \fBdocker\-mailserver\fR mount directory
(overridden by \fB\-d\fR; can also be set persistently in
\fB/etc/a2tools/a2tools.conf\fR or any file under
\fB/etc/a2tools/a2tools.conf.d/\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR a2wcrecalc (1),
.BR a2sitemgr (1)
